The [bezel set emerald cut diamond ring](/bezel-set-emerald-cut-diamond-ring) is the most protective setting format for an emerald cut stone — and the one with the most misunderstood trade-off. Most buyers choose a bezel because it looks clean and modern. Very few understand what happens to the stone's face-up size when the metal wraps the girdle.

The bezel is a continuous band of metal that surrounds the stone's perimeter at the girdle. It holds the stone in place with full contact around every edge.

For a round brilliant, this is purely a style choice. For an emerald cut, it changes something visual.

[![Bezel set emerald cut diamond ring in 14K white gold solitaire setting, overhead view showing the rectangular step-cut stone fully enclosed in a clean metal bezel](/images/bezel-set-emerald-cut-diamond-ring-white-gold-solitaire.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=bezel&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

A complete [bezel emerald cut diamond engagement ring](/bezel-set-emerald-cut-diamond-ring) starts at [$4,445](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29333987?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — a [GIA 1ct D-VS1 at $3,140](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29333987?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) plus the [Comfort Fit Bezel Solitaire 14K White Gold at $1,305](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/comfort-fit-bezel-set-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315709?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). This post covers every bezel setting that works for an emerald cut, all ring totals from entry to the [EC Side Stone Platinum at $8,400](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/bezel-set-emerald-cut-side-stone-diamond-engagement-ring-in-platinum-by-james-allen-item-304637?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), and the one trade-off you need to understand before you buy.

