## Lab Stone + Bezel Set Emerald Cut: Complete Ring Prices

Lab emerald cuts in bezel settings are the quietest category in lab diamond jewelry — and one of the best values. The bezel's clean metal surround and the lab stone's superior size-per-dollar combine into a ring that looks minimal and architectural from above but carries dramatic stone size.

The bezel's clean outline works in the buyer's favor with lab stones. A lab stone's origin is not visible to observers — no one can tell by looking at the ring whether the stone is natural or lab. But the bezel's architectural surround means the ring reads as intentional and considered, not default.

Buyers who choose a lab emerald cut in a bezel are making a specific statement: they want a large, clean step-cut table in the most protective, minimal format available. The value argument reinforces this. A natural 1ct D-VS1 in the same Comfort Fit Bezel costs [$4,445 complete](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29333987?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), while the lab 1.94ct F-VVS1 in the same setting costs [$3,534](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29147824?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — $911 less for nearly double the face-up area.

