## Best For: 4 Buyer Scenarios

**Best for active lifestyle / daily wear:** [GIA 1ct D-VS1 at $3,140](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29333987?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Comfort Fit Bezel Solitaire Platinum at $1,610](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/comfort-fit-bezel-set-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-by-james-allen-item-315706?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **$4,750 complete**. Platinum metal, full corner protection, comfort shank, 57 reviews. Built for constant wear.

**Best for budget under $4,000 (lab):** [IGI 1.94ct F-VVS1 at $2,229](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29147824?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Comfort Fit Bezel WG at $1,305](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/comfort-fit-bezel-set-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315709?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **$3,534 complete**. Near-2ct F-VVS1 emerald cut in a 57-review bezel for under $3,600.

**Best for architectural / modern design:** [GIA 1ct D-VS1 at $3,140](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29333987?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Comfort Fit Bezel Yellow Gold at $1,305](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/comfort-fit-bezel-set-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-by-james-allen-item-315674?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **$4,445 complete**. Yellow gold bezel with step-cut stone — the cleanest expression of the architectural bezel aesthetic.

**Best for emerald cut step-cut language throughout:** [GIA 1ct D-VS1 at $3,140](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29333987?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Bezel Set EC Side Stone WG at $4,300](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/bezel-set-emerald-cut-side-stone-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-304632?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **$7,440 complete**. The only setting in this dataset named specifically for the emerald cut shape, with matching step-cut side stones.

> "I tell buyers to be honest about how they wear jewelry before choosing a setting. If you take your ring off before going to the gym, the bezel and prongs are equivalent choices. If you wear your ring through everything — work, exercise, cooking, travel — the bezel is the one I'd choose every time for an emerald cut. The corners are just too vulnerable to leave unprotected on an active hand." — Farzana Hasan, **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**

